
# ---- GOLDEN FIXTURE (x11 runtime tile) ----
# resetMode=relaunch -> kill-by-pidfile + fresh Xvfb+MAME; the golden CHD is
# read-only and MAME writes an in-RAM/tile-local diff overlay, so every launch
# boots pristine (no loadvm/QMP snapshot exists for the indy_4610 driver).
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=SGI Indy (MIPS R4600) IRIX 6.5 4Dwm Indigo Magic desktop in MAME indy_4610; xl24 24-bit, exact emulated framebuffer 1288x1024; SH_CAPTURE=shm (MAME -video none) + mamesock ioport input.

# ---- CAPTURE MODE (read by x11-runtime.sh, not by the daemon) ----
# shm: MAME runs -video none — no window, no X server at all — and publishes each
# finished frame into $SH_SHM_PATH, which the daemon maps (SH_CAPTURE=shm). That
# deletes the SDL-texture + llvmpipe + X round trip the x11 mode paid for (+41%
# measured) and delivers the EXACT 1288x1024 emulated framebuffer instead of the
# 1272x954 window-scaled resample.
#
# ROLLBACK to the previous capture path is three lines: IRIX_CAPTURE=x11
# (below), SH_INPUT_BACKEND=x11test (input section below) and SH_CAPTURE=x11 in
# station.env. Nothing else changes: the Xvfb, the XTEST pointer route and the
# ImageMagick boot watchdog are all still in x11-runtime.sh and still work.
IRIX_CAPTURE=shm

# ---- POINTER/KEY INPUT (SH_* read by the daemon; the socket served by MAME) --
# mamesock = the daemon speaks mamectl/1 straight to the mamectl OSD module's
# unix control socket (issue #45): verbs ack when they APPLY, and the Lua agent
# + its 1 kHz command-file poll are gone — x11-runtime.sh (IRIX_CTL default on)
# exports MAME_CTL_SOCK and drops -autoboot_script (single-injector rule).
# ROLLBACK is one line: SH_INPUT_BACKEND=mamecmd flips the daemon back to
# appending verb lines to irix_cmd, and the launcher re-arms the module's tail
# of that file automatically (MAME_CTL_CMD_FILE) — still a single injector.
# Deep rollback (module suspect): IRIX_CTL=off restores the Lua-agent launch
# byte-for-byte; pair it with SH_INPUT_BACKEND=mamecmd.
SH_INPUT_BACKEND=mamesock
SH_MAMECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/irix/ctl.sock
# The MOVEA loop converges to this residual, in px. The module ships 2; the
# tile runs 1 because IRIX's pointer acceleration is 1:1 near zero — a single
# count IS a single pixel there — so 2 px was giving away accuracy for nothing.
MAME_CTL_DEADBAND=1
# The VC2 cursor-swap accumulators (mame-vc2-cursor-swap.patch). X programs the
# cursor register as pointer + 31 - hotspot, so swapping the cursor GLYPH forces
# a compensating write to it with the pointer standing still — and that write IS
# the hotspot, exactly. The hotspot is X server software state and sits in no
# register, so this is the only place it can be read; without it the pointer
# lands a hotspot off under every cursor but the arrow, which is why a pencil
# whose tip is at the bottom of its sprite hit the screen edge ~30 px early.
# `ctlsock: setup … swap=1` in mame.log confirms the items resolved.
MAME_CTL_SWAP_ITEMS=:vc2/0/m_cs_seq,:vc2/0/m_cs_dx,:vc2/0/m_cs_dy

# ---- GOLDEN + EMULATOR BINARY (read by x11-runtime.sh) ----
# v7 is the MERGED golden: v6's egress guest config (default route, fast-failing
# resolver, `hosts: files dns`) PLUS v4's serial exec agent (irixagent.pl on
# /dev/ttyd2, respawned from /etc/inittab), MINUS the Netscape proxy prefs — the
# host-side TLS proxy was dropped, and prefs aimed at a proxy nobody runs would
# fail every page load. md5 4f36d0b8d88e48ae02e40668b55d9a74.
# v13 (LIVE 2026-08-25, md5 319cff007fcc71d3d009e6cce51f34f0) adds the ICQ
# plane: gaim 0.64 (SGI Freeware, prebuilt -- this guest has NO compiler) plus
# its GTK2 stack, persona UIN 65000 configured against the gateway
# (proto_opts 10.99.0.2 / 5190, auto-login), seeded into every visitor account,
# started from each account's .sgisession.
#
# IT REQUIRES THE PATCHED MAME. v13 on the stock binary kills the emulator:
# a MIPS3 DRC SIGSEGV compiling gaim's first-inbound-IM code path, ~2-4 s after
# the first IM arrives. The fix is
# scripts/build-guests/patches/mame-drcfe-likely-page-end-endseq.patch
# (drcfe.ipp build_sequence dropped END_SEQUENCE with a reclaimed skip-slot
# desc). Binary md5 b0d7a0a8697c5382c287097f8799c28a; the pre-fix binary is
# kept as assets/irix/mame/sgi.pre-drcfix-20260825. Rolling the BINARY back
# means rolling the golden back to v12 too -- and either way the checkpoint
# must be recaptured, because a MAME rebuild orphans every savestate.
# docs/lab/retronet/ICQ-STATION-irix.md.
IRIX_GOLDEN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/irix/irix65-apps-v13.chd

# ---- INSTANT RESTORE (issue #44) ----
# Boot by restoring the baked MAME savestate + its pause-window-paired disk
# from $ASSETS/state/ instead of the ~390 s cold boot. x11-runtime.sh guards
# every launch: missing assets or a MAME binary whose md5 is not in the
# provenance file (a rebuild orphans every state) fall back LOUDLY to a cold
# boot, and two unhealthy restore launches in a row do the same. Rebake after
# every MAME promotion: scripts/build-guests/irix/irix-savestate/bake-golden.sh.
# Rollback is one line: IRIX_STATE= (empty) restores the cold-boot tile exactly.
IRIX_STATE=golden
# No IRIX_MAME here: the tile takes the default, mame/sgi, which since
# 2026-08-03 is the INTEGRATED build (md5 de4eb969f8ff3d72fc5b23ae23a40056) and
# does carry mame-taptun-ifname-env.patch. That patch is what makes the tap
# work at all, and an unpatched binary fails SILENTLY — it opens upstream's
# global tap-mess-<uid>-0, finds nothing and runs on with no networking. Set
# IRIX_MAME only to pin a staged binary for a bisect; `start_mame()` prints the
# tap's carrier state either way, which is the direct observation to trust.

# ---- IDLE AUTO-PAUSE (SIGSTOP arm) ----
# This tile has no QMP, so it cannot pause vCPUs the way the QEMU fleet does —
# and MAME does not care whether anyone is watching, so an unvisited exhibit
# burned ~55% of a core around the clock. SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE selects the
# daemon's other freeze mechanism: SIGSTOP the emulator itself after
# SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS with zero sessions, SIGCONT it the moment a visitor
# connects (streamhost idle.rs; labctl thaws it the same way before driving).
# Frozen is ~0% CPU and the guest's RAM/disk state is untouched, exactly like
# QMP stop; the visible trade is the same one the whole fleet already makes —
# the guest's clock stands still while nobody is there.
#
# SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH is the anti-footgun: the signal is only ever sent
# when this string appears in the pid's /proc cmdline, so a stale mame.pid whose
# pid the kernel has recycled cannot SIGSTOP an unrelated process on this box.
# indy_4610 is MAME's machine name, present in every launch this tile makes.
#
# Rollback is one line: SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=0 restores the always-running exhibit
# (the pidfile/match vars are then inert). x11-runtime.sh's two watchdogs know
# about this — mame_stopped() — and stand down while MAME is frozen, because a
# paused emulator is indistinguishable from a dead one by every signal they read.
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/irix/mame.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=indy_4610
# Warmup existed to hold the FIRST freeze until livewatch's pointer probe
# could clear the instant-restore budget (780 s = grace 600 + static-frame
# arming + the probe). Start-paused (below) moved the budget charge to the
# first observed WAKE, so an unvisited launch charges nothing and there is
# nothing left to hold the freeze for: 0 (and the launcher freezes at launch
# anyway). The one behaviour this trades away: a COLD-BOOT fallback launch now
# freezes ~60 s in when unvisited — the same mid-boot pause every QEMU tile
# accepts (idle.rs) — and the first visitor watches the rest of the boot live.
# Cold boot is the loud, rare fallback; accepted.
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_WARMUP_SECS=0

# ---- TRUE START-PAUSED (read by x11-runtime.sh; 2026-08-11) ----
# The launcher freezes the emulator at the restored golden the moment the
# restored frame is visible in shm (~5-7 s into ExecStartPre, before the
# daemon can accept a session), so `systemctl start streamhost@irix` ends
# SIGSTOPped at ~0 CPU with the desktop already painted; the first visitor
# session's unconditional cont (idle.rs) wakes it — the QEMU fleet's
# `-loadvm golden -S` (instant-ready), translated to MAME. The instant-restore
# budget charge moves with the exposure: livewatch charges .state-tries at the
# first wake it observes (one-shot .state-unvetted marker) and its pointer
# probe clears it, so unvisited restarts can never ratchet the budget into the
# 390 s cold-boot fallback. Watchdog relaunches and --mame-only still launch
# RUNNING and charge at launch (a relaunch can happen under a live visitor).
# Rollback is one line: IRIX_START_PAUSED=off restores the run-then-freeze
# launch — but restore SH_IDLE_PAUSE_WARMUP_SECS=780 above WITH it, or an
# unvisited launch is frozen before livewatch's probe can vet it and the
# budget decay this section retired comes back.
IRIX_START_PAUSED=on

# MAME is a single-threaded software MIPS emulator that will happily saturate
# whatever core it lands on, and the lab box is shared with build/benchmark
# agents. Pin the exhibit to one physical core + its SMT sibling (labhost:
# physical core 2 = logical 2,10). Unset = unpinned.
IRIX_CPUS=2,10

# ---- GUEST NETWORKING (read by x11-runtime.sh, not by the daemon) ----
# on = attach the emulated SEEQ 80C03 to a host tap. WHICH tap — and therefore
# what the guest can reach — is IRIX_NET_MODE, and the two modes are opposites:
#
#   retronet (LIVE since 2026-08-24) — rn-tapnet.sh enslaves irixrn0 to
#     vmbr-rn, the retronet bridge, which has `bridge-ports none` and NO uplink.
#     The guest is 10.99.0.24/24 with NO default route and reaches exactly one
#     host: the gateway CT 10.99.0.2 — wildcard DNS, the :80 corpus origin, and
#     OSCAR :5190. It cannot reach the LAN, the internet, labhost's own
#     listeners (the IRIXRN-IN guard chain drops every NEW flow it starts toward
#     the box) or anything else, and nothing outside the bridge can reach IT.
#     docs/lab/retronet/WEB-STATION-irix.md.
#
#   sandbox (the historical exhibit, the rollback) — tapnet.sh's host-only /30
#     point-to-point tap irixtap0 (172.31.20.1 <-> .2), with the SEPARATE
#     IRIX_NET_EGRESS decision on top: off = reach the host end and nothing
#     else; on = DIAL OUT to the LAN and the internet through a masquerade,
#     nothing dialling in.
#
# This is a 2003 IRIX with a root-owned Apache in it and seven passwordless
# accounts — the reason this tile has an interface rather than a bridge to the
# LAN, in either mode.
#
# Rollback is TWO lines, and it needs the matching golden: IRIX_NET_MODE=sandbox
# + IRIX_NET_EGRESS=on restores the internet exhibit, but only with a v9-or-
# earlier IRIX_GOLDEN — v10's guest config has no default route and resolves
# against 10.99.0.2, so it is inert on the sandbox link (which is exactly the
# containment property, stated from the guest's side). IRIX_NET=off restores the
# no-network exhibit exactly: not one MAME argument changes.
IRIX_NET=on
IRIX_NET_MODE=retronet
# The tap, its address and the helper are DEFAULTED PER MODE by x11-runtime.sh
# (retronet: irixrn0 / 10.99.0.24 / rn-tapnet.sh). They are deliberately not
# pinned here: an IRIX_TAP_IF left over from the sandbox link would silently
# override the mode and put the guest back on a /30 the golden no longer knows
# how to address.

# ---- OUTBOUND EGRESS (the second decision — sandbox mode ONLY) ----
# Meaningless on the retronet link and REFUSED there: vmbr-rn has no uplink to
# masquerade out of, so x11-runtime.sh fails the launch rather than start a
# station whose config claims an egress it does not have.
#
# What the retronet retires, stated plainly: from 2026-08-03 to 2026-08-24 this
# guest could ping 1.1.1.1 and telnet to telehack.com (an explicit operator
# decision, verified adversarially at the time — the guest's 30+ root listeners
# stayed unreachable throughout). The retronet is offline by construction
# (docs/lab/RETRONET-BRIEF.md §1: stations reach the gateway's local services
# and nothing else), so joining it replaces that NAT with the corpus. The
# exhibit trades the live internet for a 1990s one that is actually period-
# correct on a 1993 Indy — and the sandbox rollback above brings the old one
# back.
IRIX_NET_EGRESS=off
# There is no host-side web proxy and there never was one on this link either
# (dropped by user decision 2026-08-03). Netscape 4.8a connects DIRECTLY; on the
# retronet the gateway's wildcard DNS is what makes every name resolve, so a
# proxy would be a second naming layer aimed at a port this station never uses.
# https:// still fails at the handshake (4.8a's SSL 2/3 + an expired root
# store) — and on the retronet nothing serves https anyway.

# ---- GUEST AUDIO (IRIX_AUDIO read by x11-runtime.sh, SH_* by the daemon) ----
# on = MAME actually mixes sound (-sound sdl -audiodriver disk) and SDL
# write()s the raw S16LE 2ch 48 kHz PCM into the tile's audio.fifo; the daemon
# (SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo) is the CLOCK — it reads exactly 192,000 B/s and the
# pipe's backpressure paces SDL — and Opus-encodes into the same 48 k stereo
# audio track every QEMU tile uses (zero SPA changes). The launcher arms two
# guarantees before MAME starts: MAME inherits SIGPIPE ignored AND an O_RDWR
# reader-of-last-resort fd on the FIFO, so a dead or restarting daemon can
# never kill the exhibit — the 16 KiB pipe (~85 ms) fills and SDL's audio
# thread blocks while emulation continues. The daemon gates digital silence
# (>=500 ms under threshold stops audio packets; any louder frame unmutes
# instantly), so an idle desktop costs no audio bandwidth.
# Rollback is two lines: IRIX_AUDIO=off (not one MAME argument changes) and
# SH_AUDIO=off. SH_AUDIO_BITRATE keeps its 96000 default.
IRIX_AUDIO=on
SH_AUDIO=on
SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo
SH_AUDIO_FIFO=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/irix/audio.fifo
